  "comments": "<p>The Milner's Tower was built in 1871 by the residents of Port Erin in honuor of William Milner, a Liverpool safemaker. The tower was built in the shape of a lock in honour of Milner wha was a great benefactor of the town. The tower was meant to be built in secret as a surprise, but once Milner found out he donated much of the building cost.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>2016 coins has been minted without the PM mintmark even they were still produced by Pobjoy Mint.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>2008 coins have two variants of AA die letters.&nbsp;</p><p>On first variant right A is shorter and closer to the line above, distance to rim is bigger:</p><p><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/68e52e063fb1d.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/68e52e063fb1d.jpg\"></a></p><p>On second variant the right A is same size as first one and it's located little lower, shorter distance to rim:</p><p><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/68e52e2d498a6.jpg\"></p>",
